result:
Fixed in both call sites.

**Cause:** `SocketAddr::from_abstract_name` takes the abstract *name* and prepends the NUL that marks the Linux abstract namespace. Tokio detected an abstract path by checking `starts_with(b"\0")` but then passed the whole string — NUL included — to `from_abstract_name`, so `"\0aaa"` was registered as the abstract name `"\0aaa"` (`sun_path` = `"\0\0aaa"`) instead of `"aaa"`.

**Fix** (`tokio/src/net/unix/stream.rs:78` in `UnixStream::connect`, `tokio/src/net/unix/listener.rs:82` in `UnixListener::bind`) — `strip_prefix` replaces the `starts_with` check so the detection and the stripping can't drift apart:

```rust
let os_str_bytes = path.as_ref().as_os_str().as_bytes();
if let Some(name) = os_str_bytes.strip_prefix(b"\0") {
    // `from_abstract_name` prepends the null byte that marks the
    // abstract namespace itself, so it must not be passed along.
    StdSocketAddr::from_abstract_name(name)?
} else {
    StdSocketAddr::from_pathname(path)?
}
```

`from_abstract_name` had no other call sites. `abstract_socket_name` now passes, along with the rest of `uds_stream`, `uds_datagram`, `uds_split`, and `uds_cred` (22 tests, 0 failures).
